-- title:
--   Igusa valuation centre lies strictly inside a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ be primes with $\ell \ne q$, and let $M' \ne 0$ be an integer divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$, assumed to admit a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) at level $(q\ell)^2 M'$ for the subgroup $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $(q\ell)\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, with $\xi$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating $\mathfrak{m}_A$; let $A$ act on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), assumed nonzero, and write $C =$ `chartAlgFin` $A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K$ such that: an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$; $C \subseteq V$; and $V$ is residually transcendental on $C$, in the sense that some $c \in C$ satisfies $p(c) \in V \setminus \mathfrak{m}_V$ for every monic $p \in A[X]$. Then there is a maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ with $\varpi \in y'$ such that: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y'$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$; every $b \in C$ whose image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ lies in $y'$; and some $b \in y'$ has image outside $\mathfrak{m}_V$. Thus $C \cap \mathfrak{m}_V \subsetneq y'$.
--
--   The geometric content is that every irreducible component of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the modular curve meets the supersingular locus inside that chart: the centre of an Igusa-type valuation of $K$ is a non-maximal prime of the chart algebra, strictly contained in a supersingular closed point of the fibre over $\varpi$. It feeds the analysis of Igusa components at level $q$, being used in the construction of the relevant prime of the blown-up chart and in the invariance of the Igusa valuation under level automorphisms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_isMaximal_mem_ssJSet_centre_le_of_igusaValuation.lean

